ANALYTICAL INSIGHT:
Random's Δfrac mean is NOT 0 at high fire rates because P(C|¬F) variance grows.
With trace-fire-rate r, n_NF = n(1-r). At r=0.9, n_NF = 0.1n → SE(P(C|¬F)) blows up.
If incorrect-base-rate ≠ 0.5, the random gate is biased toward sign of (0.5 − EM).

Empirical bias sign vs (0.5 − EM) — predicted positive Δfrac when EM < 0.5:
  phi     EM=36.1%  →  predicted bias sign: +  observed at r=0.80: +0.1108
  gemma   EM=48.5%  →  predicted bias sign: +  observed at r=0.80: +0.5176
  qwen    EM=59.4%  →  predicted bias sign: −  observed at r=0.80: +0.1367

